            "review_title": "Review at Banh Mi 24",
            "review_text": "MaxManila\nManila, Philippines3292 contributions\n0\nVietnamese Sandwich\nDec 2019 • Family\nOne of the more popular foods to visitors in Vietnam, Banh Mi is sandwich infused with culture. French influence is very evident in the baguette bread and the liver pate. Local culture can be seen in the different types of meat that make up the sandwich or the banh mi. There is also coriander, cucumber and special sweet and spicy sauce inside the sandwich which adds much zest. \n\nI was so used to the 12-in baguette back home, so this 6-8 inch version of Banh Mi 24 is a welcome surprise. Meal is not overly heavy, and with the right amount of crunchiness and softness in the baguette.\n\nIt’s basically a take away food so enjoy it while walking on the busy streets of Ho Chi Minh. Very good heavy snack or light lunch / dinner. I don’t mind having banh mi every now and then. I\nRead more\nWritten January 5, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-13",
